  "Question": "The graph of an inverse proportional function passes through \\((-2,3)\\). Find its formula. Which of the following is correct?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y=6/x\\)",
    "B": "\\(y=-3/(2x)\\)",
    "C": "\\(y=-2/(3x)\\)",
    "D": "\\(y=-6/x\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let \\(y=k/x\\). Substituting \\((-2,3)\\) gives \\(k=-2\\times3=-6\\), so \\(y=-6/x\\). Choice A omits the negative sign.",
